<title>GERMANY: German Jan/March coffee imports up from year ago.</title>
<headline>German Jan/March coffee imports up from year ago.</headline>
<dateline>HAMBURG 1997-07-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>German net green coffee imports from outside the European Union totalled 3.37 million bags in January/March 1997 after 2.90 million bags in the same period last year, the DKV coffee association said.</p>
<p>March imports were 982,094 bags compared with 1.13 million in February 1997 and 1.18 million in March 1996.</p>
<p>Leading suppliers in March were listed in the following order -- Colombia 190,651 bags (229,449 in February), Brazil 151,122 (201,623), El Salvador 125,081 (101,012), Vietnam 85,600 (94,222) and Uganda 56,097 (49,758).</p>
<p>Honduras, which in February was in fifth position with 63,250 bags, only came tenth in March with 38,958.</p>
<p>--Hamburg newsroom +49-04-41903275</p>
</text>
